DataCare Hospital Management System

Hospital management system for Netcare Alberton Hospital (IIE WIL project, Task 2).
It consists of an Android app, a hosted REST API, and a relational database.

Architecture

Android app (Kotlin, Retrofit)
→ REST API (Node.js / Express 5) hosted on Azure App Service
→ PostgreSQL database (Supabase)

Authentication uses Firebase Authentication (email/password and Google sign-in).
The API verifies each Firebase ID token and enforces role-based access.

Repository structure

| Folder | Contents |
|---|---|
| `android-app/` | Android Studio project (Kotlin) |
| `api/` | Node.js REST API and Jest tests |
| `db/` | `schema.sql` (tables and seed data) and `reset.sql` |
| `web/` | Task 1 web prototype |
| `docs/` | Documentation and screenshots |
| `.github/workflows/` | GitHub Actions (tests and Azure deployment) |

Features

- Register, login, forgot password, Google single sign-on
- Passwords are stored encrypted by Firebase Authentication
- Roles: admin, doctor, billing clerk, patient
- Profile and settings screens (dark mode, notifications, language, change password, logout)
- Patients and appointments (double booking is rejected)
- Prescriptions: priced invoice created automatically, stock is reduced
- My Bills: pay an invoice, "Payment successful" (simulated payment)
- Notifications and an in-app help screen
- Input validation on the app and the API, with clear error messages

Hosted API

Base URL: `https://datacare-api-gtbedgf2h9ajf5c0.centralindia-01.azurewebsites.net/api/`

Health checks: `/health` and `/health/db`

Main endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/auth/sync` | Link the Firebase user to the database |
| GET/PUT | `/users/me`, `/users/me/settings` | Profile and settings |
| GET/POST/PUT/DELETE | `/patients` | Patient records |
| GET | `/doctors`, `/medications`, `/services` | Lookup data |
| GET/POST | `/appointments` | Appointments (409 if double booked) |
| POST | `/prescriptions` | Create prescription and invoice |
| GET | `/invoices`, `/invoices/mine`, `/invoices/:id` | Invoices |
| POST | `/invoices/:id/pay` | Pay an invoice |
| GET | `/notifications` | Notifications |
| GET | `/reports/summary` | Summary report |

All endpoints except the health checks need the header
`Authorization: Bearer <Firebase ID token>`.

Running locally

API
```bash
cd api
npm install
npm start
```
Create `api/.env` with `DATABASE_URL=<your connection string>` and your Firebase
service account settings. **Never commit `.env` or `serviceAccountKey.json`.**

Tests
```bash
cd api
npm test
```

### Database
Run `db/schema.sql` in the Supabase SQL editor to create the tables and seed data.
`db/reset.sql` drops everything and must only be used to start again.

Android app
1. Open `android-app/` in Android Studio.
2. Add your own `google-services.json` to `android-app/app/`. It is not in Git.
3. Run on a real phone (USB debugging on).

Automated testing and deployment

- `api-tests.yml` runs the Jest tests on every push and pull request to `main`.
- `main_datacare-api.yml` deploys the API to Azure App Service after a push to `main`.
- <Android build workflow name, once added>

